ty5|n|A strong current of air; a wind between a stiff breeze and a hurricane. The most violent gales are called tempests. ; A moderate current of air; a breeze. ; A state of excitement, passion, or hilarity. ; A song or story. ; A plant of the genus Myrica, growing in wet places, and strongly resembling the bayberry. The sweet gale (Myrica Gale) is found both in Europe and in America. ; The payment of a rent or annuity.	a:w78,106,3~w78,106,3
